{%- comment -%}
  Everything under the buy box, as ONE PAGE.

  THIS REPLACES `product-tabs.liquid`, deleted 2026-09-13 on instruction: the
  four tabs — Details, Size & fit, Fabric & care, Shipping — were shown in a
  screenshot and the answer was "itu ga usah deh, dibikin 1 page aja". So the
  panels are sections of a page now, each under its own heading, all of them
  readable without operating anything.

  It is worth knowing what was given up, because the tabs were not lazy work:
  they were real ARIA tabs with the full keyboard contract — arrows between
  tabs, Home and End to the ends, one tab stop for the strip. None of that is
  needed now, which is the point. The behaviour went out of assets/theme.js with
  them rather than being left in unused, and `[data-tabs]` went out of the
  `scripting: none` block in theme-src/theme.css for the same reason.

  What it buys, beyond the instruction: the no-script rendering and the normal
  rendering are now the same page. The tabs had two — every panel in sequence
  with the strip removed, for a reader without script — and a page with one
  shape cannot drift between them.

  ORDER IS UNCHANGED, and it was argued for once already. Size & fit sits
  second, ahead of care: the brief lists the size chart before care
  instructions, and PRODUCT.md records fit as the purchase decision itself —
  almost every one of the twenty customer reviews names a height and a weight
  before it names a size. Moving it down is a change to what the page
  prioritises, not a tidy-up.

  THE SIZE CHART HAS TWO SOURCES AND THE PER-PRODUCT ONE WINS. `custom.size_chart`
  is a rich-text metafield a product can carry for a cut that does not follow the
  house measurements; with none, `size-guide.liquid` renders the shared chart
  from theme settings. That precedence is the same shape as the Shopee link's —
  the specific beats the general, and the general is a courtesy rather than the
  intended state.

  Every section renders its own labelled placeholder when its copy is blank, so
  the page keeps its height and its shape before the studio has written a word.
  `description` and `custom.care` are both blank across this catalogue on
  purpose: the design reused one generic paragraph for all eleven pieces, which
  would state a wrong inseam and a wrong fabric on most of them.

  Accepts: product, shipping (store-wide policy copy)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign size_chart = product.metafields.custom.size_chart.value
-%}

<div class="flex flex-col divide-y divide-rule border-t border-rule">
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4 py-8" aria-labelledby="detail-details">
    <h2 id="detail-details" class="text-micro uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle">
      {{ 'product.details' | t }}
    </h2>
    <div class="wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-body">
      {% render 'copy', value: product.description, label: 'product details', lines: 3 %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-7 py-8" aria-labelledby="detail-fit">
    <h2 id="detail-fit" class="text-micro uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle">
      {{ 'product.size_and_fit' | t }}
    </h2>

    {%- comment -%}
      The chart is deliberately NOT inside `wl-measure`. A measure caps the line
      length at something readable for prose, and a table of seven sizes against
      five measurements is not prose — capping it would force the columns
      narrower than the numbers and start the sideways scroll early.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h3 class="text-caption uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-muted">{{ 'product.size_chart' | t }}</h3>
      {%- if size_chart != blank -%}
        <div class="wl-table">{{ size_chart }}</div>
      {%- else -%}
        {% render 'size-guide' %}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h3 class="text-caption uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-muted">{{ 'product.fit_information' | t }}</h3>
      <div class="wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-body">
        {% render 'copy', value: product.metafields.custom.fit.value, label: 'fit information', lines: 2 %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4 py-8" aria-labelledby="detail-care">
    <h2 id="detail-care" class="text-micro uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle">
      {{ 'product.fabric_and_care' | t }}
    </h2>
    <div class="wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-body">
      {% render 'copy', value: product.metafields.custom.care.value, label: 'fabric and care', lines: 3 %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="flex flex-col gap-4 py-8" aria-labelledby="detail-shipping">
    <h2 id="detail-shipping" class="text-micro uppercase tracking-nav text-ink-subtle">
      {{ 'product.shipping' | t }}
    </h2>
    <div class="wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-body">
      {% render 'copy', value: shipping, label: 'shipping', lines: 3 %}
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
